{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02832",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 3.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.15,
      "end_seconds": 7.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.58,
      "end_seconds": 13.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Right, did the receptionist sort you out quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.67,
      "end_seconds": 17.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Yes, she was lovely about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.05,
      "end_seconds": 23.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.62,
      "end_seconds": 29.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "I'm here because of a severe sore throat on one side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.26,
      "end_seconds": 32.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.64,
      "end_seconds": 48.55,
      "duration_seconds": 14.91,
      "text": "Febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout. I'm on sodium valproate, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Hydrocortisone cream, when needed. I used to take allopurinol, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.32,
      "end_seconds": 50.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.56,
      "end_seconds": 63.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "It's been three weeks, I'm fairly sure. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.17,
      "end_seconds": 74.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.64,
      "end_seconds": 98.63,
      "duration_seconds": 21.99,
      "text": "I notice it more with swallowing. A five out of ten, I suppose. Oh, and drooling. Had that since yesterday. Oh, and a muffled voice. I did have difficulty opening my mouth at one point, you know, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.2,
      "end_seconds": 107.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Have you had a severe sore throat on one side before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.54,
      "end_seconds": 116.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.67,
      "end_seconds": 119.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Any sign of rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.33,
      "end_seconds": 121.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "No, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.76,
      "end_seconds": 125.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "And what about noisy breathing or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.93,
      "end_seconds": 129.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.03,
      "end_seconds": 134.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.79,
      "end_seconds": 138.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.76,
      "end_seconds": 142.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.59,
      "end_seconds": 147.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Gout, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.12,
      "end_seconds": 151.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Okay, is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.89,
      "end_seconds": 156.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Epilepsy, for five years. I've had eczema, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.57,
      "end_seconds": 164.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Yes, eczema is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.27,
      "end_seconds": 178.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.41,
      "end_seconds": 184.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Yes, I had an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.65,
      "end_seconds": 190.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.31,
      "end_seconds": 193.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.63,
      "end_seconds": 197.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.41,
      "end_seconds": 207.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.84,
      "end_seconds": 209.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.02,
      "end_seconds": 217.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.5,
      "end_seconds": 236.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.78,
      "end_seconds": 252.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.28,
      "end_seconds": 277.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 95 percent on room air, pressure 125 over 76. And pulse is 101 beats a minute, temperature is 39.3 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.39,
      "end_seconds": 279.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.09,
      "end_seconds": 284.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.89,
      "end_seconds": 288.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.4,
      "end_seconds": 292.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.71,
      "end_seconds": 317.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "The right tonsil is pushed towards the middle, the uvula is deviated, and the palate is swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.9,
      "end_seconds": 322.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.73,
      "end_seconds": 350.03,
      "duration_seconds": 18.3,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards a quinsy, a peritonsillar abscess. We shouldn't forget severe tonsillitis. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had a severe sore throat on one side for three weeks, and no cough or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.97,
      "end_seconds": 352.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.37,
      "end_seconds": 374.07,
      "duration_seconds": 20.7,
      "text": "An urgent ENT drainage is what I'd like next, for peritonsillar abscess. I think blood tests makes sense here, for abscess. We'll begin with benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, now, single dose. It's for peritonsillar abscess. You need to be seen by ENT today to drain it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.67,
      "end_seconds": 390.62,
      "duration_seconds": 15.95,
      "text": "Hm, okay. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like to see you again straight away. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.28,
      "end_seconds": 395.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}